# Languages
unknown

# Lyric
[Verse 1]
The score is static, the performance lives
The fermata is a gift the player gives
Duke wrote the changes and walked away
Johnny Hodges knew just when to play
You don't need Duke to tell you how to phrase
You need Duke to tell you which moment's yours to raise

[Chorus]
The tensor is the score, the fleet is the band
The score constrains, the performer answers
The constraint that disappears is the one that works
When the orchestra's in the pocket, nobody counts
The score recedes, the music mounts

[Verse 2]
The deadband filter keeps most beats still
Only significant ones cross the hill
Duke's approach, made structural:
Transmit only what's substantial
Write the changes, trust the band
Carry only notes that demand

[Bridge]
INT8 saturation is the mixer board
No clipping, no swallowing, each voice accorded
Values clip at zero and two-fifty-five
The saturation boundary keeps alive

[Outro]
The notes on the page are not the song
But without them, nothing to sing
We read the same silent page
And the silence is everything<|endoftext|>
